</ul>

</div>

</section>
    <section class="faq" id="faq">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2>Common questions before you launch.</h2>
          <p>Short answers for planning, safety, gear, food, and weather calls.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-grid">
          <article class="faq-item is-open">
            <button type="button"><span>Do I need to bring rods and reels?</span><span>+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer">No. Premium rod and reel rentals, trolling lures, specialized jigs, and heavy-duty setups are included. You can still bring a favorite personal rod if you want.</div>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <button type="button"><span>Can more than four people join?</span><span>+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer">No. The boat is capped at four total guests, whether fishing or spectating, to preserve deck space, safety, and the private charter experience.</div>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <button type="button"><span>Are food and drinks provided?</span><span>+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer">Food and beverages are bring-your-own. The charter provides a commercial-grade marine cooler packed with fresh ice.</div>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <button type="button"><span>What happens if weather is unsafe?</span><span>+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer">If the Captain deems sea conditions unsafe, guests can choose a priority reschedule date or an unconditional 100% refund of the deposit.</div>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <button type="button"><span>Can we keep the fish?</span><span>+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer">Yes. Your catch belongs to you. The crew bleeds, washes, ices, and helps bag the fish when you return to Hadsan Beach Park.</div>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <button type="button"><span>Is trip media included?</span><span>+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer">Yes. GoPro Hero 13 and DJI Osmo Action 4 media documentation is complimentary, with raw footage and hero photos transferred after docking.</div>
          </article>

          <article class="faq-item">

<button type="button">
<span>Are accommodations available?</span>
<span>+</span>
</button>

<div class="faq-answer">
Yes. Hadsan Beach Park offers comfortable overnight rooms
for anglers who want to stay near the launch point before
early departures.
</div>

</article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="booking" id="book">
      <div class="section-inner booking-layout">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Launch from Hadsan Beach Park</p>
          <h2>Lock your private offshore date.</h2>
          <p>Send Mesopelagic Anglers your preferred date, package, session, and angler count. A 50% deposit secures the calendar slot, with the balance settled before boarding.</p>
          <ul class="policy-list">
            <li>Arrive 15 minutes before departure at the Hadsan boat ramp.</li>
            <li>100% refund for client cancellations 7 or more days before departure.</li>
            <li>On-site rooms, coffee, restaurants, and guarded parking are available at Hadsan Beach Park.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <aside class="booking-panel" aria-label="Booking details">
          <dl>
            <div>
              <dt>Community</dt>
              <dd>Mesopelagic Anglers on Facebook</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Base of Operations</dt>
              <dd>Hadsan Beach Park, Lapu-Lapu City, Mactan, Cebu</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
                      <dt>GCash</dt>
                      <dd>09177073079</dd>

                      <dt>BPI Account</dt>
                      <dd>Alex P. Senagan</dd>

                      <dd>1179048112</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <a class="primary-btn" href="https://www.facebook.com/search/top?q=Mesopelagic%20Anglers">Message on Facebook</a>

        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <div class="section-inner">
      <strong>Mesopelagic Anglers Fishing Charters</strong>
      <span>Private Cebu sportfishing charters from Hadsan Beach Park.</span>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script>
    const rates = {
      tier1: { day: 34328, night: 44626.40, full: 51492 },
      tier2: { day: 43736, night: 56856.80, full: 65604 }
    };

    const peso = new Intl.NumberFormat("en-PH", {
      style: "currency",
      currency: "PHP",
      maximumFractionDigits: 2
    });

    const packageSelect = document.querySelector("#packageSelect");
    const sessionSelect = document.querySelector("#sessionSelect");
    const anglerInput = document.querySelector("#anglerInput");
    const quoteTotal = document.querySelector("#quoteTotal");
    const quotePerson = document.querySelector("#quotePerson");
    const quoteDeposit = document.querySelector("#quoteDeposit");

    function updateQuote() {
      const anglers = Math.min(4, Math.max(1, Number(anglerInput.value) || 1));
      anglerInput.value = anglers;
      const total = rates[packageSelect.value][sessionSelect.value];
      quoteTotal.textContent = peso.format(total);
      quotePerson.textContent = peso.format(total / anglers);
      quoteDeposit.textContent = peso.format(total / 2);
    }

    [packageSelect, sessionSelect, anglerInput].forEach((control) => {
      control.addEventListener("input", updateQuote);
      control.addEventListener("change", updateQuote);
    });
    updateQuote();

    document.querySelectorAll(".faq-item button").forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const item = button.closest(".faq-item");
        item.classList.toggle("is-open");
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
